It is recommended to upload single-person images for better recognition results;
It is recommended to use images where the character's clothing color clearly contrasts with the background;
When generating emotes, it is recommended to use images where the face is fully within the frame, facing the camera, with clear facial features;
When generating actions, it is recommended to use images where the character's full body is visible;
It is recommended to shoot in a bright and open environment; dim or shadowy areas may yield poor results;
A resolution greater than 720P is recommended, with the face occupying more than 10% of the frame;
Currently supports images in .png/.jpg/.jpeg/.bmp/.heic formats.

Upload a video clip or an image and our AI will extract one of the element you choose -- [Moves, Expressions, and Camera Angles] (none of which can identify you) -- to create a short in-game animation or emote. 
Your clip or image is encrypted and automatically erased [7] days after the animation/emote is made—just long enough for us to fix any rare glitches if you report them. It is never used for model training.
